 # Generative and GAN-Based Methods
 
-Also called: Generative Radiance Fields, 3D GANs, GAN-based NeRF
 
 ## Overview
-Generative and GAN-Based Methods synthesize novel 3D objects or scenes by optimizing a radiance field to match the distribution of a pretrained 2D Generative Adversarial Network (GAN) or by directly training a generative radiance field with adversarial losses [S1]. Unlike standard NeRF which reconstructs a specific static scene from images, these methods generate new instances by sampling latent codes, enabling data augmentation and novel view synthesis of unseen objects [S1]. They differ from their siblings by incorporating adversarial training objectives or by lifting 2D GAN priors into 3D representations, rather than relying solely on photometric reconstruction losses [S1].
