 ## Shared principles
-The core mechanism involves a generator network $g_\theta$ that maps a latent code $z$ and camera pose $\xi$ to a radiance field representation, which is then rendered into 2D images. The training process typically involves an adversarial loop where a discriminator distinguishes between real and generated images, guiding the generator to produce photorealistic outputs [S1].
