 ## Background
-The field emerged from the need to generate diverse 3D data for tasks like autonomous driving and object detection, where labeled 3D data is scarce. Early 3D GANs suffered from resolution limits and 3D inconsistency [S1]. Lift3D [S1] introduced the "inverted" pipeline of lifting 2D GANs to 3D, while GOF [S1] addressed surface ambiguity in generative radiance fields by using occupancy-based rendering. These methods are primarily used for data augmentation in 3D perception tasks [S1].
